&lt;p&gt;At IMC, technology is not a department; it’s at the heart of everything we do. Developed in-house, our innovative software makes millions of trading decisions daily, and we win by making better and faster decisions than our competition. Our on-site IT Support team helps us move at a higher pace and quality each day, from hands-on support for end users to configuring and automating our systems to scale our support capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this fully on-site position, you are the first person people come to with any IT issue, whether it’s a MacBook, a SaaS application, identity and access management, or hardware and AV. You support our growing Zug office and act as first- to third-line support. Our environment is predominantly macOS and cloud-based, with a small Windows footprint. You’ll work across a wide range of SaaS and custom systems. To succeed and grow, you take ownership, work autonomously, and keep improving an IT environment that runs smoothly and is ready to scale.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;First-to-third line support for our users, mainly on macOS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing and supporting our end-user platform, including Microsoft 365, Okta (SSO, MFA, lifecycle management), Slack and the Atlassian stack (Jira, Confluence, Jira Service Management).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Device management and patching: Jamf for macOS and Intune for phones, including enrollment, configuration profiles, app deployment and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Onboarding and offboarding, including account provisioning, access management and device setup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Installing, setting up and servicing hardware and peripherals, including laptops, monitors, printers, and audio and video conferencing systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshooting, escalating and documenting network and connectivity issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automating repetitive tasks and keeping knowledge base articles and runbooks in Confluence up to date.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organizing and performing desk moves, room setups and physical equipment moves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Everything else that keeps us moving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Skills and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree in an ICT-related field (BSc level ideally), or an equivalent qualification such as Informatiker/in EFZ.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least one year of experience in a similar role in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong macOS knowledge and hands-on experience with JAMF (Pro).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Microsoft 365 administration and Intune; working knowledge of Windows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Okta or a similar identity provider (SSO, SCIM, MFA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience administering or supporting Slack and the Atlassian suite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scripting experience (Bash, Zsh, Python or PowerShell) is a plus, and so is Linux experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent troubleshooting and diagnostic skills, with the ability to solve problems creatively and proactively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to take on physical tasks such as desk moves and room setups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong drive to grow (at IMC we are committed to helping with that).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work autonomously, with a sense of urgency, and prioritize based on business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Available and willing to work on-site full-time in Zug.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in written and spoken English; German is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
